<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wartburg Festival</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1817">1817</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Wartburgfest</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wartburg">Wartburg</a> Festival was a gathering of about 500 German students at the Wartburg castle near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eisenach">Eisenach</a> on 18 October 1817, marking the 300th anniversary of Luther's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a> and the fourth anniversary of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-leipzig">Battle of Leipzig</a>. Students called for national unity and burned books they considered reactionary. Together with later events, it alarmed the German governments and contributed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carlsbad-decrees">Carlsbad Decrees</a> of 1819.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wartburg-festival.jpg" alt="Wartburg Festival" width="320" height="279" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wartburg_demonstration_1817.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
